# Repository-wide generated Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
apps/padiem-chat/.b66-worker-src/

# Local OCR model provisioning evidence (#2828). Model weights and the
# provisioning notes that reference them are local evidence, never source.
.ocr-provisioning/

# A hard-killed OCR child may leave a derived canonical PNG behind. Keep that
# local residue out of source control even if the child cannot unlink it.
kagent-ocr-*.png

# #3108: the isolated local KAgent test environment is a build artifact of
# scripts/kagent_local_test.py, created inside the checkout on purpose so its
# import origins can be proved against this repository. It is never source.
.kagent-local-test-env/

# #3108: the sibling distributions are installed with `pip install -e`, which
# still writes a setuptools build tree and egg-info next to each package even
# though the import resolves to the source. Scoped to the exact three
# distributions the launcher installs -- a repository-wide `build/` would hide
# unrelated future build directories across the monorepo.
packages/padiem-ai-core/build/
packages/padiem-ai-core/*.egg-info/
packages/padiem-control-plane/build/
packages/padiem-control-plane/*.egg-info/
apps/padiem-ai-engine/clients/python/build/
apps/padiem-ai-engine/clients/python/*.egg-info/
# #5638: committed build/lib under korean-ai-code-agent shadows src on install (setuptools reuses stale build/lib).
apps/korean-ai-code-agent/build/
# #4139 per-PC Cloudflare staging DB UUID overlay; never commit.
apps/padiem-chat/wrangler.connector-acceptance-4139.local.toml
# Wrangler account cache created by read-only ops queries; never commit.
.wrangler/

# #5231: regenerable local artifacts must never re-enter Git tracking.
# `.tmp/` is the browser-QA output directory of the `.github/scripts/b62_*`
# scripts; each CI job already uploads its own directory as an Actions
# artifact, so a tracked copy is never the canonical evidence.
# `.workbuddy-ai/` holds per-day local agent memory, `.freebuff/` is local
# agent-tool state, and `_synccheck/` is one-off operational scratch (local
# diagnostic scripts, run logs, and issue-comment drafts already posted).
.tmp/
.workbuddy-ai/
.freebuff/
_synccheck/

# #5231: the single tracked file under `padiem-reports/` is registered public
# evidence. These two directories are output directories written by the CI
# scripts that own them and are re-created on every run.
padiem-reports/2026-10-06/b66-pdf-preview-parity/
padiem-reports/b66-shell-cgi-v2/

# #5967: 대표가 전달한 디자인 원본 PNG와 생성 원본 PNG는 공개 검토가 끝날 때까지 비공개로 유지한다.
# 화면에 나가는 파생본만 reference/padiem-parliament-ai-design-v1/assets/ 에 추적된다.
reference/design-assets/
reference/generated-assets/

# #5573: the connect program's build output. The reviewed bytes travel inside
# apps/padiem-chat/app/pc_pairing_connect_exe_asset.py (base64 with its SHA-256 in
# the same file), so a second copy of the artifact in Git would only be a copy that
# can drift - and never the thing a PC downloads.
scripts/pc_pairing/connect-exe/dist/

# #5573 stage 2: the local CPython run's database, disk-R2 folder and its
# generated dev session key. All three are machine-local run state, never source.
apps/padiem-chat/local_dev_data/
